<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Catalog>

    <!-- =====================================================================
         TARDIGRADE: UPGRADE BUTTONS THE ROSTER DRAFT MUST NOT HIDE

         RosterEnforce.galaxy disables every undrafted unit with
         TechTreeUnitAllow(player, unitType, false). Blizzard's melee data
         gates a handful of UPGRADE buttons on exactly that flag, through
         CRequirementAllowUnit nodes, on the theory that an upgrade is clutter
         if you cannot build the unit it was designed for. In ladder no unit is
         ever disallowed, so those gates never fire. Here they fire constantly,
         and the button is not merely greyed out - the gate sits on the
         requirement's *Show* node and the buttons are State="Restricted", so
         the button does not render at all and the command card looks empty.

         There are exactly five CRequirementAllowUnit nodes in the whole melee
         dependency chain (Phoenix, Marine, Colossus, Immortal, Observer). Three
         are left alone deliberately:
           - AllowUnitColossus gates Extended Thermal Lance, which only the
             Colossus uses. Hiding it with the Colossus undrafted is correct.
           - AllowUnitObserver gates Gravitic Booster, likewise - and the
             Observer is not in the draft pool at all, so it never fires.
           - AllowUnitImmortal gates LearnIncreasedRange, which no live
             CAbilResearch button references any more.

         The two below are wrong for this mod and are patched by pointing the
         Show node at the same requirement minus its AllowUnit operand. The
         Use nodes are untouched, so the real tech prerequisites (Fleet Beacon
         for level 2/3, previous level complete, Tech Lab for Stimpack) all
         still apply exactly as in ladder.
    ===================================================================== -->

    <!-- The reported bug. All six Cybernetics Core air upgrades were gated on
         AllowUnitPhoenix, so a Protoss player who drafted Tempest / Void Ray /
         Carrier / Oracle but NOT the Phoenix got an empty upgrade card and no
         way to upgrade their air army at all. The Phoenix is simply Blizzard's
         stand-in for "can this player build anything that flies" - it is the
         cheapest Cybernetics-tier air unit - and that shorthand does not
         survive a drafted roster.

         Each Show node keeps its EqCountUpgrade...QueuedOrBetter0 half, which
         is what makes levels 1/2/3 share one command-card cell: a level's
         button hides once that level is queued or researched, revealing the
         next. Dropping only the AllowUnit half leaves that intact. -->
    <CRequirement id="LearnProtossAirWeapon1">
        <NodeArray index="Show" Link="EqCountUpgradeProtossAirWeaponsLevel1QueuedOrBetter0"/>
    </CRequirement>
    <CRequirement id="LearnProtossAirWeapon2">
        <NodeArray index="Show" Link="EqCountUpgradeProtossAirWeaponsLevel2QueuedOrBetter0"/>
    </CRequirement>
    <CRequirement id="LearnProtossAirWeapon3">
        <NodeArray index="Show" Link="EqCountUpgradeProtossAirWeaponsLevel3QueuedOrBetter0"/>
    </CRequirement>
    <CRequirement id="LearnProtossAirArmor1">
        <NodeArray index="Show" Link="EqCountUpgradeProtossAirArmorsLevel1QueuedOrBetter0"/>
    </CRequirement>
    <CRequirement id="LearnProtossAirArmor2">
        <NodeArray index="Show" Link="EqCountUpgradeProtossAirArmorsLevel2QueuedOrBetter0"/>
    </CRequirement>
    <CRequirement id="LearnProtossAirArmor3">
        <NodeArray index="Show" Link="EqCountUpgradeProtossAirArmorsLevel3QueuedOrBetter0"/>
    </CRequirement>

    <!-- Same failure on Terran: Stimpack was gated on AllowUnitMarine, but the
         Marauder stims too. A roster of Marauder without Marine lost Stimpack
         entirely. Show keeps its "hide once researched" half. -->
    <CRequirement id="LearnStimpack">
        <NodeArray index="Show" Link="NotCountUpgradeStimpackQueuedOrBetter"/>
    </CRequirement>

</Catalog>
